ver there's no denying its legacy  and anime fans of all ages know of the  never aging kid detective  it doesn't even baffle me as to why the  series has endured the test of time  detective conan overall is a fun show  yeah i mean a lot of times it runs off a  pattern the mysteries and cases are  quite varied enough though  and each series of episodes can be a joy  to watch as you try to solve the cases  alongside our genius protagonist and his  friends detective conan is the  definition of a time sink if you've seen  one but it's one that has some excellent  and well-written episodes to help you  exercise your mental prowess  it's really designed to be a show  without a foreseeable end because of how  open it is  and that my friends is the secret to its  longevity  next on the list is log horizon  elder tales a vr mmo featuring a  post-apocalyptic earth where magic and  fantasy have overcome the modern  technology that we've grown comfortable  with it sounds like a really cool game  to play right that is  until you find yourself trapped inside  and able to log out with no way to get  out of the game  the players must then learn how to get  accustomed to this new world well  at least death's not permanent and you  have a brainy strategic protagonist this  time around  that is log horizon in a nutshell  trapped in a video game has been a tried  and true concept for quite some time now  but i think that log horizon especially  excels among those because of a few key  things while the previous shows  generally show more of the action  aspects of a video game lock horizon is  more focused on world building the focus  isn't on escaping but more on exploring  the world and settling into the new  reality found inside  elder tale along with that comes some  really amazing moments of character and  world development and it's the whole  exploration of the host of rules and  societies that makes log horizon its own  brand of exciting if you're up for an  isakai slash video game show and are  tired of all these  power fantasy saturating the genre then  this anime  is the one for you and with the new  season airing this season it's a perfect  time to catch up with log horizontally  on the contrary now if you're craving a  genius protagonist in an over-the-top  power fantasy it's a guy  no game no life is the show for you i  basically summarize no game no life for  you but to elaborate more the story  revolves around sora and shiro  siblings known as blank gods of games  the real world is just too boring for  them so they found themselves falling  into the colorful world of disboard a  realm where fighting is not allowed  and all conflicts are to be settled with  games finding themselves the champions  of humanity the humans and the weakest  among the 16 races in the world the  siblings set off to fight for humanity's  future and to eventually challenge the  world's god itself along the way they  meet friends and foes that will push  their gaming skills to the limit if  you're up for power fantasy  fan service overload and just some over  the top action  you can't go wrong with no game no life  it's just an amazing show  that pretty much embodies all those  polarizing traits of the modern isekai  including  the painful lack of a season 2 but hey  at least you've got a movie  one of the best anime titans i've  watched mind you to make up for it  on the other hand if what you want is  more world building  and actual education from the geniuses  of the anime world you might want to  check out dr stone  how will the world end some say that it  will end in a bank consumed by fire  others have quite the different  perspectives such as the one in dr stone  in dr stone the world comes to an  end through petrification with the  entire human race being turned to stone  and eternity later daiju breaks free  from his stone prison to meet up with  his old friend  sengku being the lone survivors of the  human race the two moved to set senko's  grand plan